        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore: address gollaw code health audit findings (#293)",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nSystematic code health audit of wacli using [gollaw](https://github.com/dovocoder/gollaw) static analyzer. This PR reduces gollaw findings from **762 → 193** (−75%) through a combination of code refactoring and analyzer improvements.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Code Refactoring (wacli)\n\n**Round 1 — Helper extraction:**\n- Extracted `lockedClient()` / `connectedClient()` helpers in `client.go` — eliminated 46 duplicate mutex-guard patterns across 6 files\n- Refactored 5 largest functions: `BackfillHistory` (190→88L), `storeParsedMessage` (169→67L), `Sync` (155→~60L), `extractBusinessText` (144→<50L), `sendFile` (159→71L)\n- Unexported 13 internal symbols (api-surface reduction)\n\n**Round 2 — CLI command constructors (opencode):**\n- Extracted `RunE` logic from 10 cobra command constructors into separate `run*` functions + options structs\n- `newSendTextCmd` 127→91L, `newSyncCmd` 125→75L, `newSendFileCmd` 121→83L, `newSendStatusCmd` 119→53L, `newMessagesForwardCmd` 116→44L, `newStoreCleanupCmd` 113→39L, `runDoctorChecks` 110→38L, `newSendVoiceCmd` 109→71L, `newPollVoteCmd` 108→67L, `newSendStickerCmd` 104→67L\n\n### Analyzer Improvements (gollaw)\n\nFixed 7 analyzers to reduce false positives:\n- **Deadcode** (372→3): Fixed main/init collection, synthetic init, Store instruction tracing, generic Origin() tracking\n- **Security** (3→0): Skip `fmt.Sprintf` in error/log context\n- **Thin-wrapper** (69→6): Skip methods, error predicates, stdlib wrappers, factories, row converters, cobra subcommands, default-parameter wrappers, third-party adapters, semantic aliases\n- **Naming** (4→0): Skip standard Go initialisms (DB, WA, API, etc.)\n- **API-surface** (31→17): Skip generated files (sqlc, mockgen)\n- **Large-functions** (81→39): Use statement count + line count threshold\n- **Churn** (41→30): Exclude non-source files (docs, configs, changelogs)\n- **Unused-members** (11→8): Skip generated structs/interfaces, built-in interfaces\n\n## Impact\n\n| Metric | Before | After | Change |\n|--------|--------|-------|--------|\n| Total findings | 762 | 193 | −75% |\n| Critical | 4 | 0 | −100% |\n| Warnings | 501 | 65 | −87% |\n| Deadcode | 372 | 3 | −99% |\n| Security | 3 | 0 | −100% |\n| Thin-wrappers | 69 | 6 | −91% |\n| Duplication | 89 | 57 | −36% |\n| Large-functions | 83 | 39 | −53% |\n\n## Testing\n\nFull gate passes: `pnpm format:check && pnpm lint && pnpm test && pnpm build`\n\n## Remaining Findings (193)\n\n- 57 duplication (send commands share delegate/retry patterns)\n- 39 large-functions (cobra constructors with real logic)\n- 30 churn (git metric on source files — not fixable with code)\n- 21 complexity (info-level)\n- 17 api-surface (internal package types)\n- 8 unused-members, 6 thin-wrappers, 4 hotspots, 4 feature-flags, 3 deadcode (test-only), 3 unused-files, 1 unused-deps\n",
